# S6 (#1175), for the integration build's window (fix-walk-pending-image):
# the sign-in at the page's close against a service that accepts and stalls.
# 1. On the guest: a listener on loopback :443 (the window's tls-probe.py with
#    its handler sleeping 120 s before answering), /etc/hosts pointing
#    retroachievements.org at it, dummy credentials only.
# 2. RETROACHIEVEMENTS SETTINGS: change USERNAME to another dummy, back out.
#    Frames every second for 20 s: the menu closes at once and the carousel
#    answers input throughout (the page no longer waits); within 15 s the
#    dialog COULDN'T REACH RETROACHIEVEMENTS TO SIGN YOU IN.
# 3. Change the account again before the first answer comes: es_log.txt says
#    "a sign-in answered for an account that has changed since"; system.cfg's
#    token is empty.
# 4. Change USERNAME, open OFFLINE ACHIEVEMENTS (BETA) without closing, start a
#    scan: system.cfg carries the new name and no token from the old account.
# 5. Stop the listener by PID; restore /etc/hosts through its target.
